Bundled packages
================

Third-party Lisp belongs in lisp/vendor/<package>/.  Keep each package's
prefix, file split and license headers.  Own packages live directly under
lisp/; C sources belong under native/, outside the Lisp compilation tree.

Each import is a hard fork without history: first copy source and ERT suites
verbatim, recording source path, HEAD commit, version and license in the
commit message, then adapt in a separate commit (at most 2,500 changed lines).
Verify the first commit against a SHA-256 source manifest.  Do not import
*-autoloads.el, *-pkg.el, .elc, .so, private fixtures, Makefiles or flakes.
Existing suites go in test/lisp/<package>/; keep support files beside them.

VENDOR format
-------------

Every third-party package directory contains a plain-text VENDOR file:

  Upstream: https://example.org/project
  Version: <upstream release, or unreleased>
  Commit: <full upstream commit ID>
  License: <SPDX expression matching the retained source headers>
  Local changes:
  - None (verbatim import).

Replace the last entry with a short list of adaptations as they land.
This file documents provenance; no checker or package manager reads it.
Add each imported package to the list below with its version and license.

Imported third-party packages
-----------------------------

markdown-mode 2.9-alpha — GPL-3.0-or-later.
websocket 1.16 — GPL-2.0-or-later.
fsm 0.2.1 — GPL-2.0-or-later. See fsm/VENDOR.

Native boundary
---------------

jabber-omemo-core is the single temporary dynamic-module exception to the
Rust-native boundary.  Its source belongs in native/jabber-omemo/ and its
built module in libexec/romacs/.  R5 replaces it with the native OMEMO engine.
Never import the built .so into this tree.  epdfinfo is a separate helper
process, built from native/epdfinfo/ into libexec/romacs/.

Verification
------------

scripts/gate packages [PKG...] builds the runtime and runs each named
package's test/lisp/<package>/*.el files in a separate ERT batch process and
private HOME.  With no names it selects bundled packages with suites; core
ERT directories and resource fixtures are not selected implicitly.  Nested resource directories are not loaded as suites.  Each failing
suite is rerun under GNU Emacs 32 as a diagnostic oracle, with a fresh HOME;
GNU agreement does not turn the failure green.  Logs and exit codes are
kept in the gate run directory.  Empty suites and timeouts fail.

scripts/gate full also runs J0-batch.  It reads top-level (provide 'FEATURE)
forms in the bundled own-package paths, vendor/ and profile/, then requires
those features with the compiled runtime.  Source syntax is read by Lisp,
not inferred from filenames.  New own-package locations must be added to
BUNDLED_DIRS or BUNDLED_FILES in scripts/gate.  Profile files must contain no
autoload cookies: loading the personal profile remains an explicit choice
in the user's init.  J0 checks it explicitly in an isolated batch process.

The package tier is separate from full.  Run it whenever changing a package
or its tests, and for core integration from W4b onward.  No personal state,
accounts, live editor sessions or sockets are needed by this tier.
